    "459:1..360": "HTTP surrender/negotiation forms carry raw spokesman u64, revision u32 and optional accept bool; AnswerOffer checks Some before the helper defaults false. Demand legitimately omits an answer. Internal actor APIs retain raw character IDs before native RPC; exact canonical owners/native DB admission remain dependencies. Native accept/turn-in response booleans express serialized success, while raw i32 reward carries currency meaning from backend contract into response state. Requested and Executed outcomes are distinguished. Failed reward query falls back0 before report_contract; whether a successful report can then display0 needs actual DB/receipt policy, not an ordinary wrong-reward assertion. Abandon errors are ignored and route redirects; this is a policy question, not numeric proof of success.",
    "459:361..720": "Travel/track use authenticated session IDs, typed PartyAction and native RPC. store_battle_loot independently filters malformed CSV item IDs as u64 and quantities as u32, then sends parallel arrays455..473. Different dropped positions can leave equal lengths but change pairing: IDs11,x,22 and quantities3,4,x become11/22 with3/4. Actual canonical UI and native reducer contracts/current source still need reading. This HTTP first failure is distinct from a downstream zip-length defect unless exact alias proof establishes otherwise. Bandage form has raw patient ID/membership revision, typed Bandage enum and native SATS Option arguments; raw false is native protocol choice. Generated/manual case modes intentionally differ in tactical availability. Recovery notice uses condition-selector f32 and threshold.001 to choose cause text; exact condition units/legibility policy require owning producer. Cause strings and resource-blocked boolean derivation are separate string/shape contracts.",
    "459:721..1260": "Corpse action kind is typed, with revision and confirm-unauthorized native arguments selected by variant; absence of irrelevant fields is legitimate. Rest admission calls actual travel_rest_minutes and shelter validation before RPC, but their bodies remain dependencies. Case rendering checks owner-scoped exact site and both character/party occupancy before page construction. Nearby settlements sort raw distance and truncate5 for presentation; selected terrain plan is requested only for a listed destination. Raw distance, duration, stake, calories and fatigue fields remain application state before native/UI boundaries. Rest recommendation max(calories,0)/canonical kcal-per-day \u00d71440, ceil u64, floor1 is explicit policy; finite/calorie bounds and raw unit owners need actual producers. Living member IDs feed itinerary/provision forecasts. Native missing-row errors are converted to optional/empty UI data; no ordinary invalid-data acceptance inferred.",
    "459:1261..1594": "Counterparty IDs and membership revisions propagate from native rows to presentation; selected corpse index comes from position on the same immutable Vec, so corpses[index] is source-proved safe. Readiness refresh failure or missing/failed condition explicitly sets ready=false; reject the ordinary missing-condition false-pass suspicion for actual nonempty living member paths. Empty living set policy is separate. Autoresolve checks exact authoritative current site and routes typed outcomes; primitive u64 actor and revisions still need purpose owners. offroad_journey_minutes uses raw metres /1250m-per-hour \u00d760, ceil: currently consistent with Surface::Open1250, but duplicated authority must be reconciled by exact owner/callers. case_site_position deliberately supports checked WGS84 OR explicit abstract UnboundedCoordinateE7. Do not force abstract fixtures into geographic bounds. straight_line_distance dispatches geographic haversine6371000m or abstract Euclidean\u00d71000; invalid geographic site becomes u64::MAX sentinel. Native geometric/extreme and sentinel consumer policy are conditional, not ordinary current failures.",
    "459:1595..2102": "All existing tests were read as source only, never executed. Fixture IDs7/91, revisions1, age25, difficulty1, reward10, site distance4000 and knowledge modes are explicit test data. Condition fixtures include hunger4/thirst26 versus pain.2/blood.1/fatigue.8, so these raw condition values are not universally unit fractions. Walking480, fatigue50 and zero targets/anchors have valid fixture roles. Tests cover generated/manual combat policy, exact onsite actions, occupancy, recovery guidance and member-readiness semantics. Source-string tests assert loader/call locations; they do not establish runtime or compile acceptance. Error prose is not a compatibility obligation.",
    "460:1..90 plus extension91..105": "Travel form admits raw f32 walking hours, clamps0..24, multiplies60, rounds to native u16 minutes; finite extremes/NaN policy must be chosen explicitly, with valid zero/normalization modes preserved. Time text parses hour/minute then uses existing StrategicMinuteOfDay before native getter. Actor raw ID and night bool reach RPC. CampQuery optional bool is a supported query mode. DirectDemoContractId has raw character ID plus ordinal, parsed by exact contract:errantry-puzzle:demo tags and exactly two u64 numbers, no extra segment. This complete parser tail is newly registered. Line105 is only the next derive attribute; sibling parser106+ and remaining camp UI are unread. No claimed full1246 coverage.",
    "461:original bounded union plus registered production extensions": "Combined personal ranges now cover1..535; production1..490 complete, test491..535 only a partial prefix. TerrainPlanner owns immutable pack Arc, semaphore2, timeout10s, cooperative deadline and outer timeout11s. Permit moves into the blocking task, so it is not prematurely released on async timeout. Successful plan cache is bounded128 FIFO entries; full typed profile/weather inputs are retained except coordinate key quantization to1e-5 degrees. Cache hit precedes actual419 finite/bounds/profile/weather admission. Profile and selected weather scalar fields are exact key parts; None weather maps zero and RoutingWeather default, so no arbitrary missing-weather-key failure is inferred. Quantized coordinates are not normalized before actual planner input: exact invalid/inside boundary collisions or approximate endpoint policy need source-specific proof. TerrainPlanner key ignores precipitation/temperature because actual RoutingWeather uses only ground moisture/snow/check; reject a generic weather-key omission claim for these unused inputs. Actual forage center is authoritative; eight offsets \u00b1.01 latitude/\u00b1.015 longitude classify coast>=4 or river/wet1..3 and native wetland fields. These are semantic geographic sampling/policy units, not generic count defects. TravelDestination and provision forecasts retain raw distances, elapsed times, fatigue percent, water ml, calories, quantities and boolean modes. apply_terrain_route explicitly marks straight-line estimate on absent/failing terrain; round trip requires both plans before publishing route fields. forecast inputs require all attributes/limbs/stats/schedule rows, otherwise skip forecasting; departure maximum may defaultZERO. Fatigue capacity max(endurance\u00d7chest,.01)\u00d71000 and raw schedules need canonical unit/aggregate producer contracts. Existing core forecast_itinerary body remains a dependency.",
    "462:1..273": "Actual native HTTP DB adapter uses60s request timeout,3s connect timeout,250ms slow logging, native JSON/SATS query decoding and generated-row presentation TryFrom. query_one rejects>1 and pops safely; projected queries collect all conversions before returning. Query metrics retain raw request counts and microseconds around AtomicU64; native atomic operations and elapsed.as_micros as u64 are actual measurement boundaries. Separate Acquire loads are not one coherent pair; concurrent request deltas include other activity, so per-request isolation policy must be qualified. Counter wrap and u128 narrowing remain extreme conditions, no ordinary event claimed. Metrics elapsed records send-await completion before body.text, so advertised total SQL latency scope needs explicit definition. Reducer call is an actual raw string/JSON-args native boundary and does not decode result payload. Error-code parsing delegates to canonical reducer_error. All tests were source-only injected counters3/125/425000 and clone behavior, never run. Actual SATS decoder body remains unread.",
    "463:1..136": "Actual SATS Option and unit-variant adapters map typed BodyRegion/InterventionRoute/SurgeryProcedure to native JSON sum tags. Empty None array and unit object are native format requirements, not application semantic raw-number gaps. Test some73u64 remains native scalar example. Exports/imports do not cover query builders, preparation or generated types. No Box downcast or obsolete error-prose preservation requirement.",
    "419:necessary101..267/578..947/995..1484": "Actual routing contracts now read beyond the original load-only scope. TerrainWeights publicly stores five u16 members, requires normalized sum1000 only via is_normalized/debug_assert at arithmetic, and default is allzero. from_cover clamps source percentages to100 and produces normalized partition; with_ground_moisture preserves partition and supports independent saturation. Therefore raw canopy byte>100 does NOT inevitably create malformed route weights: this narrows013. Public/default/Serde malformed mixture policy remains qualified separately. Skill profile<=5000 and weather<=10000/5000 are checked at public pack/A* entrypoints. Pack planning checks all four finite coordinates and pack bounds before grid construction; cache461 hit bypasses this lower gate. Grid coarsens30m by1.25 until width\u00d7height<=750000, samples<=9\u00b2 cells, snaps radius8, excludes noncrossing water and diagonal corner cutting. Native numerical raw vectors/indices/costs are legitimate kernel representations; application RoutePoint/Plan/Span retain raw geographic/grid values, metre distances, seconds/minutes, per-mille multipliers and ranks. One RoutePoint type holds grid coordinates during reconstruct and geographic coordinates after plan_window transforms them: exact frame-role ownership is required. A* kernel accepts public RoutingGrid widths/metres without an explicit finite bounded-grid witness; actual WindowGrid has the750000-cell bound. Wide cost products (heuristic and step_seconds base\u00d7uphill\u00d7wet\u00d7snow before division), u32 index multiplication and reconstruction accumulations need actual grid-scale bounds/widened arithmetic. No ordinary regional overflow is established. Surface Water with crossing is passable and from speed0 uses max1; dropping Water spans at native JSON458 therefore needs explicit bridge/ferry/training policy, not a blanket impassability assumption. Distances and costs are accumulated along all n